From 2ad8f8d992842fe9648dee0e92bf0029901f5235 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: axfor <aixiaoxiang2009@hotmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 09:41:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 06/16] streamaggr: add the sum_samples_total output

sum_samples resets on every flush; sum_samples_total keeps adding sample
values and emits a cumulative counter. Where the input is already an
increment, i.e. the scrape target reports only what accrued since the last
delivered scrape, it replaces total: no previous value has to be kept per
input series, so memory does not grow with the number of inputs merged
into one output, and after a restart there is no first sample to drop as a
baseline.

The zero emitted on expiry and the leading zero of reset_marker_on_stale
apply to sum_samples_total as well.
